   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask age",
   "texto": [
    "Hvor gammel er du? means «How old are you?». In Norwegian, you literally ask «How old are you?». It is answered with er + number + år, for example Jeg er ti år.",
    "The noun år does not change in plural: ett år, ti år. In Spanish it is said «years», but in Norwegian it is not added a plural termination here."
